Package: zenith-os
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9)
Recommends: tmux
Maintainer: ZENITH/OS <zenith@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/shopEngineering/zenith
Description: ZENITH/OS — local control room for Claude Code
 A zero-dependency Python stdlib web app that serves a browser dashboard over
 your real on-disk Claude Code data: session transcripts, projects, docs,
 memories, coordination state, and a headless job runner. Runs entirely on
 localhost. Uses the system python3 (no bundled interpreter).
 .
 After install, run `zenith` to start the server and open it in your browser,
 or `zenith autostart` to keep it running as a per-user systemd service.
 Claude Code (the `claude` CLI) must be installed and logged in separately.
